<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dessert Recipes • Packers Game Day</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../recipes.css"></head><body><header><div class="kicker">4TH QUARTER • Game Day</div><h1>Dessert Recipes</h1><p>The sweet finish before Lambeau.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="backline"><a href="../recipes.html">← All Game Day Recipes</a></div><div class="section-head"><div class="tag">4TH QUARTER</div><h2>Dessert</h2><p>5 recipes in this round.</p></div><details class="recipe" id="brown-butter-chocolate-chip-skillet-cookie-frozen-custard" data-title="Brown Butter Chocolate-Chip Skillet Cookie + Frozen Custard"><summary><span class="recipe-title">Brown Butter Chocolate-Chip Skillet Cookie + Frozen Custard</span><span class="open-label">Open Recipe ↓</span></summary><div class="recipe-body"><div class="meta"><div><span>Serves</span>4–6</div><div><span>Total Time</span>45 minutes</div><div><span>Difficulty</span>Moderate</div><div><span>Equipment</span>10-inch cast-iron skillet; saucepan.</div></div><div class="makeahead"><strong>Make-ahead:</strong> Make dough up to 2 days ahead. Brown the butter earlier if desired.</div><div class="cols"><div><h3>Ingredients</h3><ul><li>8 tbsp unsalted butter</li><li>1/2 cup packed brown sugar</li><li>1/3 cup granulated sugar</li><li>1 large egg</li><li>1 tsp vanilla</li><li>1 1/4 cups all-purpose flour</li><li>1/2 tsp baking soda</li><li>1/2 tsp kosher salt</li><li>1 cup semisweet chocolate chips</li><li>Vanilla frozen custard</li><li>Hot fudge</li><li>Caramel sauce</li><li>Flaky salt, optional</li></ul></div><div><h3>Step-by-step</h3><ol><li>Heat oven to 350°F.</li><li>Melt butter in a light-colored saucepan over medium heat. Continue cooking, swirling often, until the milk solids turn amber and smell nutty, 4–6 minutes. Cool 10 minutes.</li><li>Whisk brown butter with both sugars. Whisk in egg and vanilla.</li><li>Stir in flour, baking soda and salt just until combined, then fold in chocolate chips.</li><li>Press dough evenly into a lightly greased 10-inch cast-iron skillet.</li><li>Bake 18–24 minutes. The edges should be browned, but the center should still look slightly soft.</li><li>Cool 8–10 minutes so the center sets without becoming dry.</li><li>Top warm wedges—or the whole skillet—with vanilla frozen custard, hot fudge, caramel and a tiny pinch of flaky salt.</li></ol></div></div><div class="note"><strong>KaySo note:</strong> For the best texture, pull it earlier than feels natural. A skillet cookie continues cooking from residual heat.</div><div class="recipe-actions"><button data-share-recipe>↗ Share Recipe</button><button data-copy-recipe>Copy Recipe</button><span class="status"></span></div></div></details><details class="recipe" id="monster-cookie-frozen-custard-sandwiches" data-title="Monster Cookie Frozen-Custard Sandwiches"><summary><span class="recipe-title">Monster Cookie Frozen-Cu